    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's weird. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the person looking back. like the version of me that actually mattered, the one everyone cared about and reached out to... that person is just gone. it's like i'm just a ghost walking around in a body that doesn't even belong to me anymore. everything feels so hollow.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very common feeling to feel like a stranger in your own life, especially when you've been through something that makes you question your worth. You're not alone in feeling this way, and it often means you're trying to find a version of yourself that is still real and valuable. The person who mattered is still inside you, even if you can't see them right now, so keep looking for them in the small moments that still bring you joy.",
