    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing... i don't think they're \"inside\" me. it feels more like they actually died. like the social part of me, the part that felt alive, just evaporated. now it's just this shell performing tasks, pretending to be a person. it's exhausting to keep up the charade of being alive when the real me is already gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a terrifying realization to feel like your core self has vanished, leaving behind only a hollow shell that must pretend to be whole. This exhaustion is a natural reaction to the pain of losing the version of you that once felt vibrant and connected to others. Please remember that even if the \"real\" you is gone, the one who is still here is capable of finding new ways to feel alive and meaningful.",
